Near miss for step_spacing: with an identifier limit (`nMax:STEP 2`) the
glued :STEP parses as member access on the limit, so step_spacing must
NOT fire and unexpected_token reports the header with the hint
"(missing space before ':STEP'?)". The :FOR block still opens, so no
block-pairing noise follows (diag.step_spacing, diag.unexpected_token).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE OddTotal;
	:PARAMETERS nMax;
	:DECLARE nIdx, nTotal;
	nTotal := 0;
	:FOR nIdx := 1 :TO nMax:STEP 2;
		nTotal := nTotal + nIdx;
	:NEXT;
	:RETURN nTotal;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE OddTotal;
	:PARAMETERS nMax;
	:DECLARE nIdx, nTotal;
	nTotal := 0;
	:FOR nIdx := 1 :TO nMax:STEP 2;
		nTotal := nTotal + nIdx;
	:NEXT;
	:RETURN nTotal;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
5:31-5:32 error unexpected_token: Unexpected number '2' in ':FOR' header - expected ':STEP' or ';' (missing space before ':STEP'?)
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
